    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Pustet's Ratisbon edition of the Medicaea melody; Commune pro nec Virgine nec Martyre. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of the Internet Archive scans of pp. [70]-[71] (October 2026), written as square notation on the edition's four-line staff with its C clef.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">GR</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">1884 (Editio Ratisbonensis)</idno>
            <ptr target="https://archive.org/details/gradualedetempor0000cath"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Printed edition, not a manuscript: Pustet's Ratisbon edition of the Medicaea melody of 1614, the Roman chant book until the Vatican edition; Commune pro nec Virgine nec Martyre, pp. [70]–[71].</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="title">Graduale de tempore et de sanctis juxta ritum Sanctae Romanae Ecclesiae cum cantu Pauli V. Pont. Max. jussu reformato, Ratisbon edition (imprint Rome, 1884)</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Read note by note from the Internet Archive scans (item gradualedetempor0000cath, leaves n591–n592) by two independent readers, October 2026; see research/diffusa-est/staff-readings/README.md.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
